            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imagine a bee circling close enough that its sound fills the air. You already know క, the dot-like ం, and the long ా sign. One rare first letter will turn those familiar pieces into a name for that sound."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ఝంకారం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఝంకారం — jhaṅkāraṁ — \"a buzz\" or \"a hum\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say it in three pieces: jhaṅ, kā, raṁ. The first sound is an aspirated jh, with a small breath after the voice. Read the word as ఝం-కా-రం."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is a learned, literary word derived from Sanskrit. Older dictionaries also give it a wider sense of a loud resonant noise. Keep today's image narrow: the steady buzzing or humming sound, especially the sound of a bee."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You can hear and say the whole word before the next lesson asks your hand to isolate its uncommon first letter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
