              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఝ — jha."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In ఝంకారం (jhaṅkāraṁ), the dot-like ం closes the first syllable: ఝం. Remove that sign and the base letter is ఝ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This aspirated letter is uncommon in everyday Telugu vocabulary. That is why the book gave you ఝంకారం (jhaṅkāraṁ) before asking you to practise the shape."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing: ఝ — five movements, five runs",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Follow the filmstrip slowly. Movements 1–3 travel clockwise through the three round sections. Movement 4 curls upward through the flourish above them. Movement 5 draws the separate stem downward beneath the middle-right side."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The numbered route is one attested school-style order; Telugu handwriting can vary. Keep the five pen-down runs distinct and let all three bowls stay round."
            }
          ]
        },
